  "notes": "A Dorian. thesession.org ABC (3/4, K:Edor, with chords) transposed up a 4th to A: 1-1 | 5-5 | 2-b3-2 | 1 (tied) 5-b7 | 8-b7 | 5-#6-4 | 5 (tied) 8 | 8-8 | b7-5 | 5-4-b3 | 2-b7 (tied) | 1-5 | 4-b3 | 2-1-b7 | 1 (held 2 bars). Raised 6th is F#5 in bar 7. No pickup (downbeat start). The 19-bar strain is played twice (source has a repeat) = 38 bars; ties are written as one long note. Old version was a wrong melody (it opened with a rest and A-G-E). Chords: Am Am G Am | Am Am D Am | Am Am C C | G G/B Am G | G Am Am (D major = Dorian IV). LH waltz: root quarter + 3rd/5th dyad half; final open A2+E3. The Rickheit 6/8 ABC is a different tune and was not used."
